module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a conjunct that executes, is reached, is gated on, and still discriminates nothing** (a predicate wired into a live check runs on every call, sits inside a gate that really blocks, and yet deletes cleanly: remove it and every witness stays green, because no fixture ever constructs the population that would make it false. ",

    "**It is invisible precisely BECAUSE reachability is satisfied.** The usual signature of an unenforced mechanism -- nothing calls it -- is absent, so every reachability-based tell reports health, and review reads the conjunct as a wall because it genuinely is evaluated. ",

    "Executed and enforcing are different properties, and no amount of coverage over the calling path distinguishes them. ",

    "**It is bounded against three neighbours and none of their recognition rules will find it.** `reachability_read_as_occupancy` asks whether to DELETE a guard that is quiet, and warns that mechanism-yes / join-yes / occupancy-zero is a healthy guard; this class is not about deletion and not about occupancy -- the conjunct here should stay, and the defect is that it was believed to be doing work it was not. ",

    "Section 6's inert-lens tell is machinery that nothing GATES on; this is gated on. ",

    "Section 4b's decoration case is a check whose RED cannot be authored ANYWHERE; this RED can be authored -- it simply never was, which is the whole difference, and it is the difference between a permanent ceiling and one missing fixture. ",

    "**THE REMEDY HAS TWO HALVES AND THE SECOND IS WHAT MAKES THE FIRST SOUND.** First: for each wall, run the DELETE arm and confirm EXACTLY ONE witness reddens -- not that a witness reddens. ",

    "Second: the subject that isolates the conjunct must be chosen with care, because a red for the wrong reason is how this class survives its own test. ",

    "**A THIRD HALF, AND IT IS THE MIRROR OF THE SECOND (amended 2026-09-03, tidy-koi-619 on gunbc#10257, found by warm-seal-35): CONFIRM THE DELETE ARM ACTUALLY DELETED.** The second half guards a RED for the wrong reason; this guards a GREEN for the wrong reason, and the remedy as written above is satisfiable by a no-op. ",

    "A probe that FAILED TO MUTATE and a probe whose mutation the check TOLERATED print the identical passing value, so 'run the delete arm and read the verdict' cannot distinguish a wall that holds from a wall that was never tested. ",

    "THE PROBE MUST ASSERT THAT IT MUTATED -- count the substitutions, or diff the tree -- as a claim SEPARATE from what the check then says, and then restore and re-run to confirm the green returns, because a one-sided probe does not establish that the verdict tracks the mutation at all. ",

    "SPECIMEN, and it is worth recording because both failure paths are real rather than imagined: proving the discriminating red for every_restored_stall_is_still_rostered took THREE attempts and the first two mutated nothing. ",

    "Attempt one ran the edit through `python3 -c` under DOUBLE QUOTES, so the shell consumed the escape sequences and the replacement matched no text. ",

    "Attempt two chose an anchor that matched TWICE -- the check's own pin list had just been added to the same module as the roster and repeated the same member spellings, which is a general hazard: ANY CHECK THAT ENUMERATES ROSTER MEMBERS CREATES A SECOND POPULATION WITH THE SAME SPELLINGS, so every later sweep over that module must distinguish them. ",

    "Both attempts printed the passing value and would have been read as the wall holding. ",

    "Only the third, anchored on roster-only context, dropped the row and produced the red, with the green returning after restore. ",

    "THE CATCH WAS INCIDENTAL, WHICH IS THE ARGUMENT FOR WRITING IT DOWN: the no-ops were noticed only because the edit script happened to carry an occurrence-count assertion written for an unrelated reason. ",

    "Nothing in the remedy required it. ",

    "**A FOURTH HALF, WHICH MOVES THE ROW FROM PROBE DESIGN TO READ DESIGN (2026-09-05, vivid-ibex-751, gunbc#10345): THE VERIFICATION MUTATED NOTHING, SO THERE WAS NO MUTATION TO CONFIRM.** The third half tells an author to assert that their delete arm actually deleted, and it is scoped to a probe the author CONSTRUCTS. A read-only verification has no such arm: the artifact is not modified, nothing can fail to apply, and the third half's question -- did my edit land -- has no referent. The class survives the move intact because the invalid state does not depend on there being an edit at all: **TWO HYPOTHESES, ONE OUTPUT SHAPE, AND A REGION READ THAT IS BYTE-IDENTICAL UNDER BOTH.** ",

    "**SPECIMEN OF THE READ FORM.** The claim under test was that a generated projection renders each row's FIRST receipt string. The check run was a grep for the row's bullet, confirming it BEGAN with `receipts[0]`. It did, and the claim was false: the projection concatenates ALL receipts into one bullet. A prefix match is satisfied identically by first-receipt-only and by all-receipts-concatenated, because a concatenation STARTS WITH ITS FIRST ELEMENT -- so the region inspected could not differ between the hypothesis and its negation, and the check could not have come out any other way under either. The tail was the only discriminating region and it was never read. The disconfirming bytes were present in the same file, one line further along. ",

    "**THE RECOGNITION RULE FOR THE READ FORM IS A QUESTION ABOUT THE REGION, NOT ABOUT THE PREDICATE: NAME THE BYTES THAT WOULD DIFFER IF THE CLAIM WERE FALSE, AND CHECK THAT YOUR READ COVERS THEM.** `Did I verify it` is the wrong question and it is why this passes review: the verification is real, it executes, it reads the true artifact, and it is honest. The failure is that the WINDOW was chosen where the two hypotheses agree. A structural over-approximation of the window -- read the whole record, diff the whole file -- is the cheap discharge and is usually correct; where the window must be narrow, the narrowing must be justified by naming what distinguishes it, in the same way the second half of this row demands a red be shown to fail for the intended reason. **THE TELL IS THAT THE READER CANNOT STATE WHAT THEIR CHECK WOULD PRINT IF THE CLAIM WERE FALSE**, which is the same tell this ledger records for a change detector, arriving here with no literal and no test to inspect. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, with both halves executed** (gunbc#9838, `gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier`): `census_population_is_duplicate_free` was added as a conjunct of `receipt_population_coherent`, evaluated on every coherence check and reachable from the live path; deleting it left the whole witness module green. ",

    "The fixture that isolates it is a receipt whose `refused_files` REPEATS A PATH -- enrolled as `a_receipt_whose_refused_population_repeats_a_path_is_refused_by_coherence` in `test.claim.self_host_compile_phase_frontier_witness`, with `the_same_receipt_without_the_repeat_is_coherent` as its positive control. ",

    "The subject that looks equally good and is not: a repeated ERROR DIAGNOSTIC IDENTITY also reddens the module, but it breaks a count invariant one line over rather than this conjunct, so it would have scored the DEAD conjunct as LIVE and closed the investigation with the wall still inert. ",

    "**RUNG: mechanically preventable, and the honest ceiling is the same rung rather than higher.** The unenforcing conjunct stays writable; what exists is an executed falsifier per wall, not a construction that forbids authoring one. ",

    "The next-rung trigger is a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: a mechanism that derives, from the check itself, the population its removal would change -- so that a conjunct with an empty such population fails to compile rather than waiting for an author to think of the delete arm. ",

    "Enumerating delete arms by hand does not retire it; it only executes this row's recognition rule once per wall. ",

    "**Its near twin is `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content`, and they meet from opposite sides**: there a report is complete for the REPORTER and read as complete for the SUBJECT; here a conjunct is genuinely executed and read as genuinely discriminating. ",

    "Both are the shape where the health signal the reader actually checks -- completeness there, execution here -- is fully satisfied while the property they believe it establishes does not hold. ",

    "**Neither is found by checking harder along the axis that already reads green.** **SECOND SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, the same shape one layer down and found by a different tell.** `v1.stage0.required_regen_host` `admit_stage_execution_from_model` built ONE identity list from the stage plan and passed it as BOTH the `planned` and the `executed` field of `RegenStageExecutionObservation`, so `v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction` `regen_identity_population_eq` evaluated x == x.clone() on every install of the self-host convergence transaction. ",

    "The conjunct ran, the install boundary really blocked, and `StagePlannedExecutedMismatch` stayed authorable in `v2.test.claim.regen_convergence_transaction_witness_test` while being unreachable from the real acceptance path -- the exact split section 4b's authorable-RED rule exists to catch. ",

    "**THE DELETE ARM IS NOT WHAT FOUND IT; THE PRODUCER COUNT IS**, and that is this specimen's addition to the row: reading the two sides of one population equality back to their PRODUCERS and finding a single producer is cheaper than removing the conjunct and re-running, and it needs no experiment -- any equality whose two arguments trace to one value is this class already. ",

    "**THE REPAIR IS A SECOND PRODUCER, NEVER A SECOND READ OF THE FIRST**: a digest delta over the journalled generated roster, taken before the copy loop and again after the build, carried in its own Rust newtype `ObservedEffectPopulation` with no conversion from the plan, so a later refactor cannot re-collapse the two sides without deleting a type. ",

    "Its discriminating red `stage_execution_joins_the_plan_to_independently_observed_effects` carries TWO arms because one-directional identity checking is how the loss survived: an effect on a path OUTSIDE the plan, which was green before because `allowed_after` blanket-permits every already-dirty stage0 path for the rest of the transaction; and a planned surface the stage left byte-identical, which did refuse before but as `InstalledDigestMismatch` -- a CONTENT verdict standing in for a POPULATION one, so the arm asserts the cause and not that it refused.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
